cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use volta-nvfp4, please cite it as below, and cite the upstream v100-skinny work it derives from."
title: "volta-nvfp4: NVFP4 Mixture-of-Experts inference on NVIDIA Volta (SM70)"
abstract: >-
  Extends v100-skinny's SM70 NVFP4 work to Mixture-of-Experts models via an
  expert-indirected QPN2 kernel (qpn2_moe), so NVFP4 MoE checkpoints run
  unmodified on Tesla V100 hardware that has no native FP4 or FP8 support.
  Adds a cudagraph capture ladder that removes the N>2 concurrency cliff on
  this stack, taking a 35B-A3B MoE from 39.9 to 297.7 aggregate tok/s at four
  concurrent streams on two 2017-era GPUs.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gilbertson
    given-names: Kevin
version: "1.2"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/gilby/volta-nvfp4/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gilby/volta-nvfp4"
keywords:
  - inference
  - quantization
  - NVFP4
  - mixture-of-experts
  - FP8
  - Volta
  - SM70
  - speculative-decoding
  - cuda-graphs
  - vLLM
references:
  - type: software
    title: "v100-skinny: native mixed NVFP4/FP8 LLM inference on NVIDIA Volta"
    abstract: >-
      Upstream work this project derives from. Executes Qwen3.8-27B's published
      mixed NVFP4/FP8 weight representation unchanged on SM70 (Tesla V100), via
      hand-written W4A16 (QPN2) and W8A16 (QPN8) kernels built around Volta's
      mma.sync.m8n8k4 instruction. All credit for the QPN2/QPN8 kernels and the
      SM70 NVFP4 foundation belongs to this work.
    authors:
      - family-names: Vertzyas
        given-names: Dennis
    repository-code: "https://github.com/dnv2003/v100-skinny"
    license:
      - MIT
      - Apache-2.0
